{
  "template_id": "vessel_management",
  "version": 1,
  "_help": [
    "Editable data for Settings > Vessel Settings > Folder Structure Mode.",
    "root: folder under the library root that holds the main folders; '' = library root (where existing Technical & Crewing / Commercial & Chartering / Insurance folders live).",
    "per_ship: created under <main>/<vessel name>/ for every vessel the mode is applied to.",
    "common: created once under <main>/, shared by all vessels.",
    "common_folder (optional): wrapper folder under <main>/ that holds the common folders; names follow the spec headings and the folders existing libraries already have. Remove the key to put common folders directly under <main>/.",
    "A node is {name, children?, month_driven?}; a plain string is a leaf. month_driven folders get their children inside month folders created lazily (current month by the daily job, others on upload). Month folder names use the app's existing label (ocr/dates.py month_label, e.g. 'September 2026') so uploads and the job never create two folders for one month.",
    "Names containing / \\\\ : * ? \" < > | are sanitised the same way as all other app folders (e.g. 'Flag / MPA' -> 'Flag - MPA').",
    "Matching to existing folders is case-insensitive, ignores spaces/punctuation and treats '&', 'and' and nothing as equal."
  ],
